---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import { appointmentUrl } from '../../data/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Coaching Packages | Signal & Structure Coaching"
  description="Explore coaching package options for ADHD, executive-function, student, and professional coaching."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Ways to work together"
    title="Coaching packages"
    intro="Clear options for focused support, system building, and ongoing accountability."
    crumbs={[{ label: 'Packages' }]}
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container package-intro">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Choose enough support to test the system</p>
        <h2>Real change usually needs more than one good conversation.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="measure">
        <p>
          Coaching packages create enough space to identify a problem, build
          something useful, try it in real life, and make adjustments based on
          what actually happens.
        </p>
        <p>
          The package examples below show how Signal &amp; Structure could
          organize coaching for this fictional portfolio practice.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="packages-grid">
        <article class="package">
          <div class="package-number">01</div>
          <p class="package-type">Focused support</p>
          <h2>Reset Sprint</h2>
          <p class="package-length">3 sessions · about 4 weeks</p>
          <p>
            A short coaching cycle for one specific area that has become
            difficult to manage.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>one primary coaching goal</li>
            <li>friction and workflow mapping</li>
            <li>one or two practical systems to test</li>
            <li>adjustment and next-step planning</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="best-for">
            <strong>Useful for:</strong> an overloaded calendar, a difficult
            semester transition, task initiation, or rebuilding one routine.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="package featured">
          <div class="package-number">02</div>
          <p class="package-type">Core package</p>
          <h2>Systems Build</h2>
          <p class="package-length">6 sessions · about 8–10 weeks</p>
          <p>
            More room to work across connected challenges and build systems
            that can survive an ordinary week.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>priority and workload mapping</li>
            <li>planning and capture systems</li>
            <li>task-start and transition supports</li>
            <li>weekly testing and refinement</li>
            <li>recovery planning for disrupted weeks</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="best-for">
            <strong>Useful for:</strong> adults, students, or professionals
            who want a broader executive-function system rather than a
            single-task solution.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="package">
          <div class="package-number">03</div>
          <p class="package-type">Ongoing support</p>
          <h2>Tune-Up</h2>
          <p class="package-length">2 sessions each month</p>
          <p>
            Continued coaching for people who already have useful systems and
            want regular review, accountability, and adaptation.
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>review current systems</li>
            <li>identify new friction quickly</li>
            <li>adjust plans as demands change</li>
            <li>maintain realistic accountability</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="best-for">
            <strong>Useful for:</strong> changing workloads, new responsibilities,
            ongoing school demands, or maintaining systems over time.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container included-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Across coaching packages</p>
        <h2>The goal is usable structure, not more homework.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="included-list">
        <div>
          <span>01</span>
          <strong>Collaborative planning</strong>
          <p>Build around your actual workload, energy, responsibilities, and constraints.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>02</span>
          <strong>Real-world testing</strong>
          <p>Try systems between sessions and bring back what happened rather than what was supposed to happen.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>03</span>
          <strong>Adjustment</strong>
          <p>Change tools and routines when they create more work than they remove.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>04</span>
          <strong>Recovery planning</strong>
          <p>Build systems that can restart after travel, illness, deadlines, or a difficult week.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark">
    <div class="container start-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Not sure which option fits?</p>
        <h2>Start with the problem, not the package.</h2>
        <p>
          The discovery call is meant to clarify what is difficult right now
          and what amount of support may make sense.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Button
        href={appointmentUrl}
        variant="light"
        tracking="request-appointment"
      >
        Book a discovery call
      </Button>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .package-intro,
  .included-grid,
  .start-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .packages-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .package {
    position: relative;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.4rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--sand);
    background: white;
  }

  .package.featured {
    border-top: .45rem solid var(--structure);
  }

  .package-number {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--structure);
    font-size: .7rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
  }

  .package.featured .package-number {
    color: var(--structure-dark);
  }

  .package-type {
    margin-bottom: .5rem;
    color: var(--signal-text);
    font-size: .68rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: .13em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .package h2 {
    margin-bottom: .4rem;
  }

  .package-length {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: .86rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .package ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: .65rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .package li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.35rem;
  }

  .package li:before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: .65em;
    left: 0;
    width: .5rem;
    height: .5rem;
    background: var(--signal-strong);
  }

  .best-for {
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--sand);
    font-size: .9rem;
  }

  .included-list {
    display: grid;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--sand);
  }

  .included-list > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.25rem 1fr;
    gap: .35rem 1rem;
    padding: 1.3rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sand);
  }

  .included-list span {
    grid-row: 1 / span 2;
    color: var(--structure);
    font-size: .68rem;
    font-weight: 900;
  }

  .included-list strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .included-list p {
    font-size: .92rem;
  }

  .start-grid {
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width:48rem) {
    .package-intro,
    .included-grid {
      grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr;
      gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 7rem);
    }

    .start-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width:70rem) {
    .packages-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      align-items: stretch;
    }

    .package.featured {
      transform: translateY(-1rem);
    }
  }
</style>
